    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0802" n="1636" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/400</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-22T09:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1918, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 24, 11.03 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4037. For War Trade Board [from Dresel]:</p>
                <p>No. 1001 [<hi rendition="#italic">101</hi>]. Cotton agreement has finally been
                    ratified by British, French, and Italian delegates and only awaits formal
                    acceptance by Swiss of following modification in order to take full effect.
                    British Government has ratified with reservation that total of exports under
                    heading A, B, C, and E, pages 1 and 2 of agreement, shall not exceed 300 metric
                    tons per annum. Exports for <pb facs="0803" n="1637" xml:id="pg1637"/> April,
                    May, and June this year were at approximately this rate. Instructions to French
                    delegates provide for acceptance figures for 1917.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
